On Jan 22, 2013, at 1:16 PM, Saptarshi Guha wrote:

> hello,
> 
> I'm not sure if this is possible without a custom class loader. I have a R package that adds a JAR j to the classpath and then creates an object from  a class C found in j.
> 
> I then modified the source to JAR j (specifically to class C), recompiled and would like to reload, so that the next time i create an object from class C, it reuses the modified JAR?
> 

Java doesn't support explicit unloading. The only way to unload a class is if *all* its object instances *and* the class loader get garbage-collected by Java. rJava already uses custom loader which you have access to so you could daisy-chain another instance of the rJava loader that you keep under your control, but I'm still not sure how you can make Java to garbage-collect it at the point you need it ... 

Cheers,
Simon

